  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed rear extension, by reason of its excessive depth and projection beyond the rear elevation of the adjoining property, would result in an unacceptable overbearing impact and loss of light to neighbouring habitable room windows and the rear amenity area, causing significant harm to the living conditions of the occupiers of the adjoining dwelling. Whilst the applicant's exceptional circumstances and evidenced needs are acknowledged and have been given substantial weight, these considerations do not outweigh or justify the identified harm to neighbouring residential amenity, notably No.4 Vimy Close. The proposal is therefore contrary to the Local Plan policies CC2 and intention of the Council's Residential Extension Guidelines (Part A5 of the Hounslow Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD)."
